## hungarian.rule - mangling rules for Hungarian password candidates
##
## Use with any base wordlist, e.g.:
##   hashcat -m 0 hashes.txt hungarian-passwords.txt -r rules/hungarian.rule
##   hashcat -m 0 hashes.txt ascii/names-male.txt     -r rules/hungarian.rule
##
## Covers the habits visible in real Hungarian leaks: capitalising the first
## letter, trailing ! , year suffixes centred on birth years and the
## current decade, and the usual leetspeak. Lines beginning with # are
## comments; : is the no-op (leave the word unchanged).

# keep original + simple case toggles
:
l
u
c
C

# trailing punctuation
$!
$.
$1
c $!
c $1

# year suffixes - birth years (1950-2012) are the most common PIN/suffix
$1 $9 $5 $0
$1 $9 $6 $0
$1 $9 $6 $5
$1 $9 $7 $0
$1 $9 $7 $5
$1 $9 $8 $0
$1 $9 $8 $5
$1 $9 $9 $0
$1 $9 $9 $5
$1 $9 $9 $9
$2 $0 $0 $0
$2 $0 $0 $5
$2 $0 $1 $0
$2 $0 $1 $2
c $1 $9 $8 $0
c $1 $9 $9 $0
c $2 $0 $0 $0

# current-decade suffixes
$2 $0 $2 $3
$2 $0 $2 $4
$2 $0 $2 $5
$2 $0 $2 $6
c $2 $0 $2 $4
c $2 $0 $2 $5
c $2 $0 $2 $6

# short numeric suffixes
$1 $2 $3
$1 $2 $3 $4
c $1 $2 $3

# leetspeak (Hungarian vowels included)
sa4 se3 so0 si1
se3 so0
sa@ se3
